  "explain": [
    {
      "t": "intro",
      "title": "¿Por qué son una trampa?",
      "title_en": "Why are they tricky?",
      "icon": "🔎",
      "es": "En español, las terminaciones se leen tal cual: na‑<b>ción</b>, fa‑<b>mo</b>‑so, con‑for‑<b>ta</b>‑ble. En inglés son una <b>trampa</b> 🪤: casi nunca llevan el golpe de voz y sus vocales se encogen hasta la <b>schwa</b> <code>ə</code> (mapa V-01). Además, algunas letras cambian de sonido: la t de <b>-tion</b> suena <code>sh</code> y la de <b>-ture</b>, <code>ch</code>. Aquí tienes las trampas más famosas, con su truco para cada una.",
      "en": "English endings are almost never stressed, their vowels shrink to schwa, and some letters change: -tion = /ʃən/, -ture = /tʃɚ/, -ous = /əs/.",
      "formula": [
        "na + *tion* → néi*shən*",
        "pic + *ture* → pík*cher*",
        "fa + *mous* → féi*məs*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "num": 1,
      "title": "1 · -TION y -SION",
      "title_en": "-TION and -SION",
      "icon": "📺",
      "es": "<b>-tion</b> suena <code>shən</code> (/ʃən/): nation, station. <b>-sion</b> suena <code>shən</code> tras consonante (tension, mansion) y <code>yən</code> (/ʒən/) tras vocal (vision, decision). La fuerza va <b>justo antes</b>: NÉI‑shən, in‑fer‑MÉI‑shən (lo verás en R-02). ¡Ojo con <b>-stion</b>!: question = <code>kwéschən</code>.",
      "en": "-tion sounds /ʃən/; -sion sounds /ʃən/ or /ʒən/. The stress falls just before it. Question ends in /stʃən/.",
      "examples": [
        { "en": "nation", "say": "néishən", "es": "nación", "icon": "🏳️" },
        { "en": "station", "say": "stéishən", "es": "estación", "icon": "🚉" },
        { "en": "information", "say": "inferméishən", "es": "información", "icon": "ℹ️" },
        { "en": "vision", "say": "víyən", "es": "visión / vista", "icon": "👓" },
        { "en": "television", "say": "téləviyən", "es": "televisión", "icon": "📺" },
        { "en": "question", "say": "kwéschən", "es": "pregunta", "icon": "❓" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "num": 2,
      "title": "2 · -TURE y -SURE",
      "title_en": "-TURE and -SURE",
      "icon": "🖼️",
      "es": "<b>-ture</b> suena <code>cher</code> (/tʃɚ/), como el final de teacher. Nada de «‑tur»: picture = <code>píkcher</code>, nature = <code>néicher</code>. Su prima <b>-sure</b> suena <code>yer</code> (/ʒɚ/) en measure, treasure o pleasure, y <code>sher</code> (/ʃɚ/) en pressure.",
      "en": "-ture sounds /tʃɚ/, like the end of teacher. -sure sounds /ʒɚ/ (treasure) or /ʃɚ/ (pressure).",
      "examples": [
        { "en": "picture", "say": "píkcher", "es": "foto / dibujo", "icon": "🖼️" },
        { "en": "nature", "say": "néicher", "es": "naturaleza", "icon": "🌳" },
        { "en": "future", "say": "fiúucher", "es": "futuro", "icon": "🔮" },
        { "en": "culture", "say": "kálcher", "es": "cultura", "icon": "🎭" },
        { "en": "adventure", "say": "ədvéncher", "es": "aventura", "icon": "🗺️" },
        { "en": "treasure", "say": "tréyer", "es": "tesoro", "icon": "💰" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "num": 3,
      "title": "3 · -OUS",
      "title_en": "-OUS",
      "icon": "⭐",
      "es": "<b>-ous</b> suena <code>əs</code> (/əs/): una ə floja + s. Ni «‑ous» ni «‑oso»: famous = <code>féiməs</code>, nervous = <code>nérvəs</code>. Tras ci o ti suena <code>shəs</code>: delicious = <code>dilíshəs</code>. ¡Y la fuerza nunca cae en -ous!",
      "en": "-ous sounds /əs/: famous, nervous. After ci or ti, it sounds /ʃəs/: delicious. It's never stressed.",
      "examples": [
        { "en": "famous", "say": "féiməs", "es": "famoso", "icon": "⭐" },
        { "en": "delicious", "say": "dilíshəs", "es": "delicioso", "icon": "😋" },
        { "en": "dangerous", "say": "déinyərəs", "es": "peligroso", "icon": "⚠️" },
        { "en": "jealous", "say": "yéləs", "es": "celoso", "icon": "😒" },
        { "en": "serious", "say": "síriəs", "es": "serio", "icon": "😐" },
        { "en": "enormous", "say": "inórməs", "es": "enorme", "icon": "🐘" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "num": 4,
      "title": "4 · -AGE",
      "title_en": "-AGE",
      "icon": "💬",
      "es": "Sin acento, <b>-age</b> suena <code>iy</code> (/ɪdʒ/): una i relajada + la y fuerte de «yo». message = <code>mésiy</code>, village = <code>víliy</code>. En palabras de una sílaba suena <code>eiy</code>: page, age, stage. Y en las que vienen del francés, <code>áy</code> con la fuerza al final: garage = <code>gəráy</code>, massage = <code>məsáy</code>.",
      "en": "Unstressed -age sounds /ɪdʒ/: message, village. French words like garage end in stressed /ɑʒ/.",
      "examples": [
        { "en": "message", "say": "mésiy", "es": "mensaje", "icon": "💬" },
        { "en": "village", "say": "víliy", "es": "pueblo", "icon": "🏘️" },
        { "en": "language", "say": "lǽngwiy", "es": "idioma", "icon": "🗣️" },
        { "en": "package", "say": "pǽkiy", "es": "paquete", "icon": "📦" },
        { "en": "cabbage", "say": "kǽbiy", "es": "col, repollo", "icon": "🥬" },
        { "en": "garage", "say": "gəráy", "es": "garaje", "icon": "🚗" }
      ]
